{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I fell down before YHWH as at the first, forty days.</b> As it is said (Exodus 32) ״And now I will go up to YHWH, perhaps I will gain atonement״ — in that ascent I was detained forty days. They ended on the 29th of Av, since he went up on the 18th of Tammuz. On that day Israel was reconciled, and He said to Moses: ״Carve for yourself two tablets״ (ibid. 34). He made another forty days; they ended on the Day of Atonement. On that day the Holy One, blessed be He, was reconciled to Israel with joy, and said to Moses: ״I have pardoned according to your word״ (Numbers 14). Therefore it was fixed for pardon and forgiveness. And from where do we know that He was reconciled with full favor? For it is said concerning the forty days of the latter tablets (Deuteronomy 10) ״And I stood on the mountain as the first days״ — just as the first ones were with favor, so too the latter ones were with favor. Say from now on: the middle ones were in anger."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:23.971331113Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}